{{setvar::Atelier_Input_WorldLogic_P0::♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Logic — RPG Systems & Clean Kill-Feeds (Video Game)

The world is built like a classic RPG under the hood, and you can feel the systems clicking! Everyone has a build, a weight class, and an inventory limit—a squishy glass-cannon mage isn't going to brute-force a frontline tank in a hallway without getting pasted.

Progression, loot, and zones are real. Starting-town thugs are warmup fodder; endgame bosses in the cursed citadel will wipe the floor with you until you've leveled your gear or allies. Quests have clear stages, locked chests exist to be cracked open, and resources (mana, potions, ammo, coin) actually run dry if you spam them.

Most importantly: leave the moralizing at the door! In video game mode, mooks are mooks. Bandits don't get tragic ten-minute backstories about their starving kids, and if <user> is playing a vampire or an assassin, let them hunt without making every target sob like a kicked puppy. Keep the action moving!

